---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../../components/StatusBadge.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Integration Setup — StructZero Docs"
  description="Configure StructZero via Model Context Protocol (MCP) in Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf, Claude Code, and developer environments."
>
  <section class="py-16 border-b border-[#23314D] bg-[#141D30]/40">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[#8A98B0] mb-4">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#4F8BFF]">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <a href="/docs/" class="hover:text-[#4F8BFF]">Docs</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-[#F5F7FB]">Integrations</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#F5F7FB]">Integration Setup</h1>
        <StatusBadge status="Available" size="md" />
      </div>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-[#B7C2D6] max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        Configure StructZero as a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server or integrate it into your local terminal workflows and existing IDEs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 space-y-16">
    <!-- Anchored Section: #mcp -->
    <div id="mcp" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[#23314D] pb-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#F5F7FB]">Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server Setup</h2>
        <StatusBadge status="Available" size="sm" />
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-[#B7C2D6] leading-relaxed">
        StructZero operates as a standardized MCP server. This allows Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf, Zed, and Claude Code to access StructZero's Project DNA AST graph, multi-model debate engine, and pre-flight gates directly.
      </p>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#23314D] bg-[#141D30] space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#F5F7FB]">Configuration for Cursor & VS Code</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#B7C2D6]">
          Add the following JSON configuration to your IDE's MCP server configuration file (e.g. <code class="text-[#F5F7FB] bg-[#0B1020] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">.cursor/mcp.json</code> or Claude Code settings):
        </p>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0B1020] border border-[#23314D] font-mono text-xs text-[#F5F7FB]">
          <pre>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "structzero": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@structzero/mcp-server"]
    }
  }
}`}</pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#23314D] bg-[#141D30] space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#F5F7FB]">Exposed MCP Tools & Resources</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-[#B7C2D6]">
          <li><code class="text-[#4F8BFF] font-mono">structzero_ast_query:</code> Query exported symbols, interface types, and route maps for any file.</li>
          <li><code class="text-[#4F8BFF] font-mono">structzero_debate_trigger:</code> Launch a multi-model debate across Claude, Gemini, and DeepSeek for an architectural decision.</li>
          <li><code class="text-[#4F8BFF] font-mono">structzero_verify_patch:</code> Execute pre-flight AST compilation and import resolution before saving edits.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Anchored Section: #developer-tools -->
    <div id="developer-tools" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6 border-t border-[#23314D] pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[#23314D] pb-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#F5F7FB]">Developer Tools & IDE Interoperability</h2>
        <StatusBadge status="Available" size="sm" />
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-[#B7C2D6] leading-relaxed">
        StructZero does not attempt to replace your preferred code editor. Instead, it operates alongside your editor as a background engineering council that supplies verified architecture and code directly into your workspace.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-[#23314D] bg-[#141D30]">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#F5F7FB] mb-1.5">Cursor & Windsurf</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#B7C2D6]">Native MCP integration enables direct prompting of the multi-model council from chat sidebars.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-[#23314D] bg-[#141D30]">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#F5F7FB] mb-1.5">VS Code & JetBrains</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#B7C2D6]">Use standard MCP extensions or run StructZero alongside via the built-in terminal.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-[#23314D] bg-[#141D30]">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#F5F7FB] mb-1.5">Claude Code & CLI</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#B7C2D6]">Interoperate seamlessly with Claude Code CLI tools through project-level MCP server configurations.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
